    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce __future__ Imports at File Start",
    "description" : "Ensures that __future__ imports are placed at the beginning of a Python file, before any other statements except docstrings.",
    "explanation" : "# late-future-import (F404)\nDerived from the Pyflakes linter.\n## What it does\nChecks for __future__ imports that are not located at the beginning of a\nfile.\n## Why is this bad?\nImports from __future__ must be placed the beginning of the file, before any\nother statements (apart from docstrings). The use of __future__ imports\nelsewhere is invalid and will result in a SyntaxError.\n## Example\n```\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n```\n## Use instead:\n```\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom pathlib import Path\n```",
