    "title" : "Enforce Mapping for Named Placeholders in Percent-Format Strings",
    "description" : "Ensures that named placeholders in printf-style format strings are used with mapping-type values.",
    "explanation" : "# percent-format-expected-mapping (F502)\nDerived from the Pyflakes linter.\n## What it does\nChecks for named placeholders in printf-style format strings without\nmapping-type values.\n## Why is this bad?\nWhen using named placeholders in printf-style format strings, the values\nmust be a map type (such as a dictionary). Otherwise, the expression will\nraise a TypeError.\n## Example\n```\n\"%(greeting)s, %(name)s\" % (\"Hello\", \"World\")\n```\n## Use instead:\n```\n\"%(greeting)s, %(name)s\" % {\"greeting\": \"Hello\", \"name\": \"World\"}\nOr:\n\"%s, %s\" % (\"Hello\", \"World\")\n```",
